# The ending screen in full (build 93a): the six epilogue pages, the
# strip wipe and the last picture, the text over the stars, the credits
# under "Never Dream" with their palette fade, the ending UFO, and the
# button back to the Sega screen. The way there is mother_brain_won's.
#
# Each page: its portrait slides in on plane A (page 1 from the right),
# its palette in line 2, its text typed beside it -- one code every two
# frames, the controls locked -- for 720 frames, then plane A cleared and
# 60 frames of nothing. The starfield is on plane B throughout but its
# palette line is black until the last picture's palette; the planet's
# rim lights up with the credits' palette fade, whose last step starts
# the UFO. Pixel values are from an independent composition of the ROM's
# tables (build 93a's history): Rudo's portrait $888, the planet dark
# during the pages and $600 over the stars, Rolf's picture $E66, a
# lowercase credits letter $A44 and an uppercase one $EEE, the ship $888.
# Two build 93 slips are pinned too: the music, which the ROM starts
# before its fade to white (build 93 started it 21 frames later, at the
# screen), and the fade in from white, one channel a frame, blue first
# ($6EE after four frames; build 93 stepped all three, $666). On build 93
# the music check fails first; past it, the screen was the font on black.

start level $64 33 37
party 4 50
outfit Rolf Neimet NeiSword NeiShield NeiArmor -
outfit Nei NeiCrown NeiSlasher NeiSlasher NeiCape -
outfit Rudo Neimet NeiShot NeiShot NeiArmor -
outfit Amy NeiCrown NeiSlasher NeiEmel NeiCape -
wait idle
walk up 4
wait idle
wait ticks 2
wait idle
expect script $1813
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
expect menu $1F
press c                      # YES
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
expect menu $1F
press down
press c                      # NO: "Die!"
wait idle
expect script $1818
press c
wait screen battle
expect flag $C747 1
wait idle                    # FIGHT/STGY
enemy-hp 1
press c                      # FIGHT: one hit
limit 60000
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
limit 3000
wait screen level
wait ticks 6
wait idle
expect script $183B
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
expect script $181F
press c
limit 3000
wait idle                    # three steps back, then "{char} wait!"
expect script $1831
expect level $64 33 37
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle                    # eleven north, then Lutz's warning
expect script $1832
expect music $91
expect level $64 33 26
press c
wait idle                    # seventeen north, then the Earthmen
expect script $1819
expect level $64 33 9
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
expect menu $1F
press c                      # YES: we hate you
wait idle
expect script $181A
press c
wait idle
expect script $181C
press c
wait idle
expect script $1833
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
expect menu $1F
press c                      # YES: tell us why
wait idle
expect script $1834
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
expect script $1821
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait idle
press c
wait ticks 2                 # "The Place of Death" before the white fade
expect music $93
limit 3000
wait screen ending
wait ticks 4                 # four steps down from white: blue first
shot 00_fading_in
expect pixel 0 0 $6EE
wait ticks 725
shot 01_page1
expect pixel 80 120 $888
expect pixel 300 60 $000
expect script $182A
limit 1000
wait ending page2_slide
wait ticks 3
shot 02_page2_sliding
wait ending page2_text
wait ticks 700
shot 03_page2
expect script $182B
wait ending page3_text
wait ticks 700
shot 04_page3
expect script $182C
wait ending page4_text
wait ticks 700
shot 05_page4
expect script $182D
wait ending page5_text
wait ticks 700
shot 06_page5
expect pixel 200 100 $288
expect script $182E
wait ending page6_text
wait ticks 700
shot 07_page6
expect script $182F
wait ending wipe
wait ticks 3
shot 08_strip_wipe
wait ending last_picture
wait ticks 100
shot 09_last_picture
expect pixel 160 100 $E66
wait ending final_days_text
wait ticks 600
shot 10_final_days
expect pixel 300 60 $600
expect script $1830
limit 12000
wait ending credits
expect music $97
wait ticks 4500
shot 11_credits
expect pixel 98 36 $A44
expect pixel 125 60 $EEE
wait ending ufo
wait ticks 24
shot 12_ufo
expect pixel 188 24 $EEE
expect pixel 176 24 $888
wait ending button
shot 13_the_end
expect pixel 130 96 $EEE
wait idle
press c
# (build 157a) The button's ScreenID_Sega: SegaScreen sends $E0 and fades
# the credits out (PaletteFadeFrom) before its setup, red first. The
# button's $9001 has the planes 64x32 by then, so the VDP reads plane A's
# first 32 rows: THE END stays (the port's wrap drew PRESENTED BY SEGA
# there, from rows 32-63). Until 157a the port cut to the logo's setup;
# the log has the $E0 on the press's tick. Eleven steps in, THE END's
# white has lost its red and four of its green ($E60); PRESENTED's P
# (130, 88) would be lit there.
wait ticks 10
shot 14_fading
expect pixel 130 96 $E60
expect pixel 130 88 $000
wait screen sega
expect no-stderr is not ported
